Name: VP9 coefficiant adaption
URL: https://chromium.googlesource.com/webm/libvpx/
Revision: 4d0fe85c1957cea215085e7da41ee797e6a51f01
Security Critical: yes

License File: LICENSE
  License: Apache-2.0

Description:
  This directory contains an externally provided, standalone C kernel authored by
  Amlogic, Inc. (`vp9_coefficient_adaptation.c` and `.h`) to calculate and pack
  32-bit hardware register settings for VP9 bitstream entropy probability
  coefficient and mode adaptation on Amlogic GXM/G12A video decoders.

  Provenance & Synthesis Note:
  This code does NOT exist as a standalone file in upstream `libvpx`. It was likely
  synthesized by Amlogic engineers by extracting VP9 entropy probability equations
  and unrolling syntax tree mode tables from WebM `libvpx` (`vp9_entropy.c`,
  `vp9_entropymode.c`, `vp9_entropymv.c`, and `vpx_dsp/prob.h`).

  Because the VP9 bitstream format is finalized (RFC 6386), the probability
  adaptation mathematics are standard-invariant and do not require upstream syncs.
  Comparing with the WebM project's upstream code demonstrated no functional change
  has occured as of v1.17.0-rc1
